Chess 3.18

This repository adds iPhone and iPad support to Apple's open-source
Chess.app, based on Chess-570.1. The iOS app requires iOS 13.0 or later
and a Metal-capable device. Its bundle identifier is com.apple.Chess,
and its executable and application bundle are Chess and Chess.app.

The iOS application provides a native UIKit interface around the shared
Metal renderer and chess model, with touch, pointer, keyboard and
VoiceOver support. It includes standard chess, Crazyhouse, Suicide and
Losers variants, an in-process Sjeng engine, hints, undo, move history,
board and piece styles, and configurable speech.

Named games, autosave, recent games, multiple iPad windows, and .game/PGN
import and export use the application sandbox and system document picker.
Game Center provides turn-based matches when authentication is available;
ReplayKit provides screen recording. Localized resources are included.
The original macOS project remains available in MBChess.xcodeproj.

Build the iOS application in ChessIOS.xcodeproj using the Chess scheme,
or run the following command with Xcode and ldid installed:

    ./Scripts/build-ipa.sh

This creates build/Chess.ipa with local ad-hoc signing for sideloading.
The build does not request an Apple provisioning profile. Installation
requires a sideloading method that supports this signing arrangement.
An output directory can be supplied as the script's first argument;
DEVELOPER_DIR can select an installed Xcode, and CHESS_DERIVED_DATA can
reuse an existing build cache.

